 and are skipped). For each, take its bounding box; the box is square, so its width gives the key into the table. Fill every background cell strictly inside the box with the looked‑up colour.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    out = g.copy()\n    table = {5: 8, 7: 4, 9: 3}  # frame side length -> fill colour\n    for o in objects(g, bg=bg):\n        if o[\"size\"] <= 1:\n            continue  # the centre dots\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = o[\"box\"]\n        side = x1 - x0 + 1\n        if side not in table:\n            continue\n        col = table[side]\n        inner = out[y0 + 1:y1, x0 + 1:x1]\n        inner[inner == bg] = col\n        emit(out, f\"Fill the interior of the {side}x{side} frame at ({y0},{x0}) with colour {col}, keeping its centre dot\")\n    emit(out, \"All frames filled\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"topology":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The output keeps every 2 cell unchanged and paints the empty interior of each frame with a new colour."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- 5×5 frame (3×3 interior): painted 8 (pairs 1, 3, 4)"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- 7×7 frame (5×5 interior): painted 4 (pairs 2, 3)"}],"count":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The position of the frame, the number of frames and the grid size do not matter (pair 3 has a 5×5 and a 7×7 at different places; pair 1 has a 9×9 and a 5×5)."}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"For each, take its bounding box; the box is square, so its width gives the key into the table."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"788f1c6f80a62d64b9c5cae255c8edad695f6d5226546be41f7da3b78589422c","task_sha256":"94535cf111e888cbf941cfeb907d844c347c9121340d1ab0571a1fab0c392728","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
